 "note": "One-sided defense with the base in the middle of the screen. The map is 80 x 40 cells; the player sees a 53 x 20 cell window centred on the command core, so the three entries (left x=8, right x=70, top y=0) are 4 to 10 cells outside it and wave units are already walking when they appear. One walled compound (brick ring, openings of five cells on the left, right and top, no gap at the bottom where the rhythm lane sits) with one pillbox at the end of each opening and no gun turrets or SAM sites. Each opening has a defense point 3.5 cells outside its wall. Riflemen (about 1.3 cells/s) need about 12 s from the left or right entry to its defense point and 10 s from the top, jeeps (about 4 cells/s) 4 s and 3 s (the pack build prints it per wave). Factory and barracks exits and the rally point lie inside the ring and never block the openings. Later levels add defenses through battlefield variants.",
